 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and self-consistent: generalisable matrix lemmas are public in `Matrix` with a general index type, the obsolete real test-vector scaffolding is deleted rather than aliased, and `SpinDensityC` ships a complete characteristic API (`*_def`, `ofReal_*`, both `IsTimeReversalInvariant` characterisations, `isParityInvariant_iff`, `@[ext]`, and the `timeReversalInvariantEquiv` round trip) with a confluent, correctly directed simp set. No compatibility artifacts, no `private` general infrastructure, no free data defeating extensionality.",
